{
  "$comment": "T-2.49: which line each event is said with, as data (ADR-017). An event's `lines` are voice-script lines (voices.json), said in turn; `cooldown` seconds must pass before the event is said again — by anyone in the squad, or by the same soldier when `scope` is `speaker`; `priority` decides which of two waiting radio lines goes first; `self` is whether your own soldier says it. A squadmate within `radioBeyondM` of you is heard where they stand, dry; beyond it, over the radio treatment — and only one voice is on the radio at a time: another waits up to `radioQueueSeconds` for it, `radioGapSeconds` apart, or is dropped. A soldier never starts a line within `speakerGapSeconds` of their last one ending. A line nobody has recorded yet plays `chirp`. `sight` is when an enemy is a new contact: seen within `rangeM` by a squadmate's eye, with no one having seen it for `forgetSeconds`, checked every `everySeconds`. A grenade not the squad's within `grenadeWarningM` of a squadmate is warned of; an enemy dying within `killCreditSeconds` of a squadmate's round or blast is theirs to call.",
